# Six, investment arguments

# 6.1 Look at the logic (three cores)

**1. AI is an enhanced agent rather than an alternative**
The real performance of RELX proves that AI is positive for its business. The company embedded AI in its own product, enhancing the value and pricing of analytical tools.

**2. High-quality business models are discounted significantly**
70% plus ROE, 21%+ net interest rate, 34.8% operating profit rate, continuously expanding profit rate, 87% digitalized income, and steady 7% organic growth. Assets of this quality should not be traded 16 times PE in any market.

**3. Management confidence in real silver**
Repurchases in 2025 were Pound1.5 billion, and repurchases were planned for 2026 at Pound2.250 billion.

# 6.2 Look at the empty logic (3 cores)

**1. The long-term threat of AI may be underestimated**
While RELX benefits from AI in the short term, large-scale AI models may gradually replace specialized databases and analytical tools in the long term. Google Scholar, AI legal assistants, AI risk assessment tools evolve at unpredictable rates.

**2. Academic publishing model facing structural challenges**
The opening up of access campaigns, the rise of preprint servers (e.g., arXiv) and the rebound of academia against high subscription fees may fundamentally change the business model of academic publishing. The risk of this section is not negligible.

**3. High ROE quality needs to be considered with caution**
70% plus ROE is partly lower than the shareholder equity base due to large buybacks and historical goodwill impairments. The return on actual capital input (ROIC about 24%) is excellent but far below the figure suggested by ROE. The valuation should refer more to ROIC and free cash flow rates, rather than ROE.

