# VII. Conclusion

** The contradiction between the AI panic narrative and the fundamentals is worth noting.**

RELX is a typical data monopoly: it has hard-to-replicate big data, it is embedded in its client workflows, and it is using AI to enhance its competitiveness. The real performance in 2025 (7% organic growth, profit rate expansion to 34.8%, full-line acceleration) does not support the narrative of "AI subversion".

From the valuation point of view, this may be a typical "Mr. Market's Fear" scenario:
- 16-fold forward PE buys a 70% + ROE, 7% steady growth, and profit margins continue to expand
- Management buybacks at a low level (2.25 billion pounds in the 2026 plan)

The core risk is: **Will the narrative of the AI threat be falsely corroborated over longer periods of time?** The scope for valuation restoration would be significant if RELX continued to show evidence of AI enhancements rather than substitutions in 2026-2027.

The recommendations focus on following up:
1. Have organic growth remained stable or accelerated across business lines
2. Whether profit margins continue to expand
3. Specific disclosure data on revenue from AI-related products
4. Practical impact of open access on SSM operations

